BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What Does the Supreme Court's Trans Sports Ruling Mean for Indiana
 ?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260724T100000
UID:b6ea3b4745dffd1a339c0f1769fa8e71@mobilize.us
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mobilize-uploads-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/u
 ploads/event/IMG_3811_20260701160739211787.png
DESCRIPTION:The ACLU of Indiana will host a virtual briefing on the U.S. S
 upreme Court’s ruling in West Virginia v. B.P.J. and Little v. Hecox\, a
 nd what the decision means for transgender students\, schools\, and civil 
 rights protections here in Indiana. Legal Director Ken Falk and Advocacy M
 anager Danielle Drake will discuss the ruling\, Indiana’s existing ban o
 n transgender girls participating in girls’ school sports\, and what que
 stions remain for students\, families\, schools\, and advocates.
LOCATION:Virtual event
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/acluin/event/981972/
X-SOURCE:Indivisible Central Indiana (Mobilize)
END:VEVENT
